        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Singapore Airlines, Singapore Airlines Cargo\n- Branding: Singapore Girl, Sarong Kebaya\n- People: Goh Choon Phong\n- Roles: Chief executive officer, flight attendants\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1972, Singapore Airlines flight attendants have worn the distinctive Sarong Kebaya uniform.\n- Since 1972, the Singapore Girl has been a consistent visual advertising slogan depicting Singapore Airlines flight attendants in the Sarong Kebaya uniform.\n- The Singapore Girl remains a prominent element of Singapore Airlines marketing.\n- Singapore Airlines uses the Singapore Girl as the central figure in its corporate branding.\n- Goh Choon Phong is the chief executive officer of Singapore Airlines and Singapore Airlines Cargo.",
